WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.067
-What an exciting day I had.
It's such an amazing Monday.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.667
I went -- I was at
the White House this morning.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:08.000
Hours ago,
I was at the White House.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
I went -- they invited me to go
to the Easter Egg Roll.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.934
And I go, "I would love to go."
They go, "We know you've got

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.501
the 'Nana Loves You More' book,"

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.100
and that's what
Dr. Jill Biden --

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.667
her grandkids call her Nana.
-Aww.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.234
-I go, "This is perfect."
I go, "Great.

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:25.767
Will I meet the First Lady?"
They go, "Not necessarily, no."

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.067
[ Laughter ]
I go, "Okay, I'm still honored.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.434
That would be amazing.
I'd love to go."

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:32.567
The girls -- I brought my kids.
And -- And so they go,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.367
"Yeah, it's just a thing,
you'll go.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.000
We don't know
if you'll see anyone.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.133
It's really
the First Lady's event.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.801
So, but you might see her,
but she has things to do."

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:44.234
I go, "Trust me,
I totally understand."

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.400
Went, had the best time.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.567
Got to meet everyone.
-Oh.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.667
-Got to meet President Biden.
I got to meet the First Lady.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:54.534
I saw Ashley Biden.
It was just --

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.434
We went there, and the last time
I was at the White House,

00:00:57.434 --> 00:01:01.534
I think was --
I did the Fourth of July --

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.267
I did some stand-up
for veterans.

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:04.701
And that's where
I wore like a --

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.167
I think I wore, like,
an eight-piece suit.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.200
-Yeah.
-Because I was so excited

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.334
to meet the President
and the First Lady.

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.901
I just wanted to wear
the best suit I could wear.

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.701
It was 100 degrees,
and I was sweating.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.100
[ Laughter ]
I looked terrible.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.200
I looked like I was having
a stroke for the whole day.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.868
[ Laughter ]
And I got to meet them.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.567
And finally, the sweat
was in my collar,

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.667
and Michelle Obama was like,
"Are you all right?"

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.067
President Obama was like,
"Didn't you get the memo?

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.567
This is a barbecue."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.901
And I go, "Yeah."

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.534
I go, "This time,
I'll be prepared."

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:32.934
I wore a nice kind of
lightweight suit.

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.968
-Right.
-Of course it was 40 degrees

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:36.968
in D.C. this morning.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:39.868
But I went. We went yesterday,
Easter Sunday.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.901
I went with --
And we didn't have much time.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.267
I wanted to go sightseeing
with Nancy and the girls.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:48.267
So, we just jumped --
We got a car,

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:51.267
and we just jumped out,
different spots, took a photo,

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.634
or had someone take the photo,
and then ran back in the car.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.467
This is us at the Capitol.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.934
No one looking at the camera
at all.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.634
[ Laughter ]
My eyes are closed.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:04.567
This is us -- it's the
Washington Monument right here.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.033
And the Mall.
No one looking.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.067
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.634
-No one's looking
at the camera there.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.133
-No.
-Then I got the hang of it.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.434
This one was good.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.634
This one's the Lincoln --
Lincoln Memorial.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.067
-There you go.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.667
-Yeah, that's everyone there.
But you -- what you realize

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.601
while you're doing this,
there's hundreds of people

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.100
looking at the Lincoln Memorial.
-Yeah.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.234
-But now they're staring
at you, posing.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.367
-Yeah.
-I go, "Whatever."

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:26.501
-Yeah, whatever.
-I don't want to take

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.567
anything away from Lincoln.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.534
But it was -- it was --
it was amazing.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.434
Then I just got the hang of it.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.834
This is just a nice --
a nice thing of us there.

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.000
-Aww.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.934
-Yeah, nice.
And then this is us at the --

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.968
the White House, this morning.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:44.300
And we get there --
It was just amazing.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.300
You get to --
you get to say hi, you know,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.100
and I go, "Oh, my gosh."
You go, "Hello,"

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.367
and they just -- President Biden
just kneeled down

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.434
and just talked to my girls
like, "I don't know

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.100
the man you're with,
but what are you guys up to?"

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.834
All right. You know?
He was funny.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:00.167
And the First Lady was amazing.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.300
I've never met the First Lady.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.567
Just charming
and just looked great.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:07.734
And you just feel --
It's so -- It just feels --

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.200
I don't know what it is,
in D.C., in general.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.501
If you ever get a chance,
go to D.C.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.834
Just go to Washington, D.C.
Everything's free.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.701
There's museums everywhere.
It's just --

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.901
Natural History Museum,
you got the Smithsonian.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.400
-Air and Space Museum.
-Air and Space.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.801
World War II Memor--
-Yeah.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.868
-You get to see memorials.
It's just, honestly --

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.801
And you just go,
"God, I love this country."

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.133
It's so good.

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.000
What a beautiful, amazing --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.133
The history of this place
is amazing.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.501
I loved it.
I had the best time.

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:39.300
And I go to read the book,
I go, "Great,"

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.534
and the First Lady goes out.
She goes, "I'm gonna go out --"

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.167
Somebody said the First Lady's
going to go out and read

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.200
"Brown Bear, Brown Bear."
I go, "Awesome.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.601
I'd love to even see that."

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.000
So she did it
in front of the kids.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.300
And the kids are all laughing.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.000
It was, like -- amazing, like,
educational-themed,

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.801
but fun family thing for the --
for, like, the kids.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.033
And then,
she was supposed to leave.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:00.234
And then, the President
comes and sits next to her.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:01.467
So, then
they're both sitting there,

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.567
and then I thought
they were both gonna leave.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.567
Then they go,
"We'll stay for Jimmy."

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:07.067
And so they just stayed,
and we read "Nana"

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.601
to all these kids
with the President.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.701
He was like --
and the First Lady's like --

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.534
Because, you know, it's me.
So I'm just like -- I'm --

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.534
I don't even consider myself,
really, an author.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.000
But I'm reading this book.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.067
And she's going,
"I love this book."

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.801
And I was like,
"Put her mic up."

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:22.934
[ Laughter ]
"This is fantastic.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:25.334
This is a great endorsement
or my book."

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.567
They could not
have been nicer humans.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.667
And everyone was great.
What a great vibe from there.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:30.968
I just want to thank
the White House so much

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.834
for inviting me.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.968
Go check out D.C.
if you want to go on vacation.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.467
It's a beautiful place.

